---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
// DRAFT: written by Claude for Cormac to review. Edit freely.
---
<Base title="About" description="About Cormac Madden: real-time 3D developer based in Leamington Spa, originally from Dublin.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    I'm a real-time 3D developer from Dublin, now based in Leamington Spa. I build software that takes
    real-world data (factory systems, sensors, tracked people) and turns it into something you can walk around in.
  </p>

  <h2>How I got here</h2>
  <p>
    I started out behind a camera. As a teenager I set up a small freelance business, Kuda Media, shooting video and
    photos of properties. Clients kept asking for buildings that didn't exist yet, so I learned 3D to show them, and
    spent the next few years on architectural visualisation: rendering, compositing and 360° tours.
  </p>
  <p>
    A summer in Berlin at Beyonity moved me from offline rendering into Unreal Engine, once it was clear a game engine
    could turn out the same quality of video in a fraction of the time. That was the point I got more interested in how
    the engine worked than in what it produced, so I studied Computer Science &amp; Business at Trinity College Dublin,
    then an MSc in Augmented &amp; Virtual Reality.
  </p>
  <p>
    During the MSc I worked at Algorithm, a virtual production studio, building a head-tracked LED wall with Unreal nDisplay
    and an Azure Kinect. Since 2024 I've been at JLR, building digital twins of its factories in Unity and NVIDIA Omniverse
    and the pipelines that feed them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Coming from media means I care about how things look and read, not just whether they run. Most of my work sits
    between the two: making the engineering data correct and the 3D clear enough that people actually use it.
  </p>

  <h2>Languages</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>English: native</li>
    <li>German: B1</li>
    <li>French: basic</li>
    <li>Irish</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Photography</h2>
  <p>
    Photography started as the visual side of my freelance work and stayed a hobby: mostly landscapes, cities and
    drone shots, some of them on <a href={site.links.instagram}>Instagram</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="actions"><a class="btn secondary" href={site.links.instagram}>Instagram @cormacmadden</a></p>

  <h2>Outside work</h2>
  <p>
    I've spent winters working ski seasons in the Alps and snowboard whenever I can. The rest of the year it's the gym,
    running, piano, and whatever I'm modelling in Blender that week.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or message me on <a href={site.links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
